meta {
  name: Start Attempt
  type: http
  seq: 5
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/student/assessments/attempts
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
  Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "application_id": "{{applicationId}}"
  }
}

script:post-response {
  if (res.status === 201) {
    const data = res.getBody();
    if (data.data && data.data.id) {
      bru.setEnvVar("assessmentAttemptId", data.data.id);
    }
  }
}

docs {
  Creates an AssessmentAttempt AND starts the clock in one call — status
  is "in_progress" immediately (started_at/last_activity_at set to now),
  for the WHOLE Application (covers every course listed on it) — one
  attempt per application, not one per course. There is no separate
  "begin" endpoint — the two were merged since there's no screen between
  attempt-creation and the timer running in the actual take-test flow
  (the Room screen's instructions/countdown all happen before this call).

  No slot_id — the slot is auto-resolved server-side the same way as Get
  Assessment Start Info: Application.admissionCycle.assessmentTemplateId
  -> the template's currently active slot.

  Requires: the Application belongs to the authenticated student,
  Application.formStatus is "submitted", the admission cycle's
  assessment_required is true, the admission cycle has an
  assessment_template_id set, that template has a currently active slot,
  and there's a currently approved paper_type: "normal" paper on that
  template. Fails with a 409 ConflictError if any of those aren't met
  ("This application is not currently at the assessment stage" /
  "Assessment not required for this application" / "No assessment
  configured for this admission cycle" / "No assessment slot currently
  scheduled" / "No approved paper available for this assessment yet"), or
  "You already have an attempt for this application" if one already
  exists.
}
